# Surface Pro 12 (Intel): the rear camera relay with sp12bt601 (sp12-autoframe).
# Loaded after sp12-rear.conf by the relay unit drop-in, so these values
# replace that file's. Not a .conf: v4l2-relayd's generator starts one relay
# per *.conf in this directory.
#
# icamerasrc's frames are labelled BT.709 and the loopback describes its
# frames as BT.601 matrix, sRGB transfer, BT.709 primaries, limited range
# (2:4:7:1), so the relay's output videoconvert converted every frame: about
# 30 % of a core for a change of matrix only. sp12bt601 does that change in
# place with a lookup table (about 3 ms per frame) and labels the frames
# 2:4:7:1; FORMAT carries the label into the relay's appsrc caps, and the
# videoconvert passes the frames through.
#
# sp12isplock holds /run/sp12/isp.lock while the camera is open: the front
# and rear cameras streaming through the ISP together wedge its firmware, so
# the second one waits until the first has closed (sp12-autoframe 0.9).
VIDEOSRC="icamerasrc device-name=ov13858-wf fps-range=15~30 ! video/x-raw,format=NV12,width=1920,height=1080,framerate=30/1 ! sp12isplock ! sp12bt601 ! videoconvert"
FORMAT="NV12,colorimetry=2:4:7:1"
